fpga-network-stack: the changes fRAC is built with

lib/fpga-network-stack is a git subtree of fpga-network-stack
(https://github.com/fpgasystems/fpga-network-stack), commit 68bfe24.
fRAC is built with the copy of it that EasyNet
(https://github.com/fpgasystems/Vitis_with_100Gbps_TCP-IP) carries on
branch vitis_2022_1, commit f34831d. The two differ in 15 files, and
this patch changes them to EasyNet's versions:

- CMakeLists.txt also builds hls/ipv4.
- hls/hash_table, hls/mem_utils.hpp, hls/ib_transport_protocol,
  hls/rocev2 and README.md take EasyNet's versions.
- hls/packet.hpp, hls/toe/tx_engine/tx_engine.cpp and
  hls/arp_server_subnet/CMakeLists.txt differ only in whitespace.

EasyNet's copy also leaves out upstream's test vectors, documents,
Vivado checkpoints, waveforms and .gitignore. The commit that added
this file deletes those as well; this patch does not.

The patch is already applied in this repository. From its root:

    # passes when the patch is applied, as it is here
    git apply -R --check patches/fpga-network-stack.patch
    # applies it to lib/fpga-network-stack at upstream 68bfe24
    git apply patches/fpga-network-stack.patch

In a clone of fpga-network-stack itself, add -p3.

